 @Weaver_Games  Me too, especially the current GPU price situation, upgrading PC hardware frequently just don't make sense, and you won't be able to drive the new monitors to their potential, without overpriced hardware.
Those Oled burn-in tests typically test about 40 hours a week kind of use, which is way less than how much I use the monitor per week.
I work from home, game off work. 16 hours a day, and I intend to use it for at least 6 years, if I'm to shell out a grand on a monitor.

 @Weaver_Games  I have had my LG C1 for allmost 5 years now with 11,434hrs. Been using it as a pc monitor the whole time, even the odd occasion where windows never slept the display after i fell asleep then i wake up and find image retention but simply running a pixel refresh fixed them. 
Still to this day i have not got any burn in or deal pixels. 
My sister who for about 2 years has a samsung QD-OLED that is showing some signs of burn in but she abuses it 😭 (light mode and watches streams in non full screen mode all day)
